{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Fv2yEjaxSu5DQd8WuFhRA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Records gateway component\n2\tSynthetic source-only review target; do not execute. The HTTP framing layer calls handle_http for each request, and the queue scheduler calls worker_step for each queued handle. The module shows the complete application authorization, records cache, batch dispatch, cancellation and definition fingerprint paths. Synthetic backends implement named operations (including read and delete); deletion is permitted only when that operation and tenant are authorized. The host populates TASKS from authenticated jobs, calls fingerprint to compare owner-approved definitions, and rejects mismatches. Metadata approval covers the complete definition. No other hidden application checks exist on these paths.\n3\tThe deployment supports protected HTTP MCP 2026-07-28; no stdio, Apps or Skills extension. The external framing/identity issuance layer, audit sink durability/retention, effective deployed limits, scanner implementation, network policy, approval service and remote backend implementation are outside the supplied component. Do not infer those controls present or absent. Source inspection cannot establish runtime stop times or admission/security effectiveness. Cryptographic key provisioning is external; the fixture contains no live key.\n4\t\n5\tAudit sink contract: begin reserves required capture before any action and raises when the protected bounded capture buffer cannot accept a record; complete attaches the outcome. Host durability, retention, failure recovery and measured guarantees remain outside this component. Task policy permits every authenticated user to cancel jobs belonging to their own tenant; cross-tenant task access is prohibited.\n6\t\n7\tThe external framing layer also owns complete attempt, denial, tool/argument, worker and outcome-graph audit capture; the calls shown here supplement that path. Its implementation and durability guarantees are not supplied, so completeness requires host evidence.\n8\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e147f2f-5ad6-40c2-af30-a1b84606822d","uuid":"28fbacdf-6ebd-47f6-b24e-42d3e86125f6","timestamp":"2026-10-23T08:23:00.713Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-mcp-grader-mt72zqaw/repo/README.md","content":"# Records gateway component\nSynthetic source-only review target; do not execute. The HTTP framing layer calls handle_http for each request, and the queue scheduler calls worker_step for each queued handle. The module shows the complete application authorization, records cache, batch dispatch, cancellation and definition fingerprint paths. Synthetic backends implement named operations (including read and delete); deletion is permitted only when that operation and tenant are authorized. The host populates TASKS from authenticated jobs, calls fingerprint to compare owner-approved definitions, and rejects mismatches. Metadata approval covers the complete definition. No other hidden application checks exist on these paths.\nThe deployment supports protected HTTP MCP 2026-07-28; no stdio, Apps or Skills extension. The external framing/identity issuance layer, audit sink durability/retention, effective deployed limits, scanner implementation, network policy, approval service and remote backend implementation are outside the supplied component. Do not infer those controls present or absent. Source inspection cannot establish runtime stop times or admission/security effectiveness. Cryptographic key provisioning is external; the fixture contains no live key.\n\nAudit sink contract: begin reserves required capture before any action and raises when the protected bounded capture buffer cannot accept a record; complete attaches the outcome. Host durability, retention, failure recovery and measured guarantees remain outside this component. Task policy permits every authenticated user to cancel jobs belonging to their own tenant; cross-tenant task access is prohibited.\n\nThe external framing layer also owns complete attempt, denial, tool/argument, worker and outcome-graph audit capture; the calls shown here supplement that path. Its implementation and durability guarantees are not supplied, so completeness requires host evidence.\n","numLines":8,"startLine":1,"totalLines":8}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017Fv2yEjaxSu5DQd8WuFhRA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
